==Battleground==
*4 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Baron Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Hyppoh]]s spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Mega-Mooth]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Super Hyppoh]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
In the infinite generosity of the stage designers, the bosses spawn on base hit rather than on timer. The most reasonable way to beat this stage is through [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] stacking; clear out the opening swarm of peons with a few [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] until it is just Hyppoh and Mooth left, then stall the both of them with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]]. You will ideally want at least three unsynced Cyberpunk Cats on the field before proceeding (two if his Slow [[Talents|Talent]] is fully leveled).

During the boss wave, you'll need 4-5 meatshields to "hold them back," where you will be slowly chipping them by cycling out Courier Cats, [[king Dragon Cat|king Dragon Cats]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cats]], and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Minas]] until Baron Seal dies first. Once that happens, the pressure will lessen greatly, and you can take things much more sedately. Mega Mooth will be the next one to die, and by this point there will be no substantial threat with only Super Hyppoh out on the field. Either knock her behind the base and destroy it, or kill her.

